# ── Dexvra Trade Bot — environment ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env (never commit .env) and fill in.

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather (a NEW bot, separate from the main Dexvra listing bot)
TRADEBOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC...

# REQUIRED — master secret used to AES-256-GCM encrypt every user's private key.
# Use a long random string (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`). If this leaks, every
# custodial wallet is compromised. If it CHANGES, existing wallets can't be
# decrypted — set it once and back it up securely.
WALLET_SECRET=

# Where the bot's trading fee (BOT_FEE_BPS of each trade) is sent — the Dexvra
# EVM treasury (default baked into core.js; same address on every EVM chain).
FEE_WALLET=0x212cE51eBF3162189dA1acaD0BFc0544b985f1B5
BOT_FEE_BPS=100        # 1.00% per trade
REF_SHARE_BPS=3000     # referrers earn 30% of that fee

# ── Chains ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which chains are enabled (comma-separated). One EVM key = same address on all.
ENABLED_CHAINS=robinhood,ethereum,base,bsc,arbitrum

# Robinhood Chain (home — the launchpad bonding curves live here)
RPC=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
CHAIN_ID=4663
FACTORY_ADDR=0xf0a093bc6ab5bb408ca1f084ec2161d879edaa57
DEX_ROUTER=0x89e5db8b5aa49aa85ac63f691524311aeb649eba
WETH=0x0bd7d308f8e1639fab988df18a8011f41eacad73
EXPLORER=https://explorer.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com

# ── Uniswap V3 routing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The engine auto-picks the deepest pool per token: V2 pair vs Uniswap V3 (fee
# tiers 0.01/0.05/0.3/1%). It prices/routes V3 off the pool's slot0 spot, so
# only FACTORY + ROUTER are needed (no QuoterV2 — that lets it work on custom V3
# forks whose quoter doesn't match). Ethereum/Base/BSC/Arbitrum ship with the
# canonical addresses baked in. Robinhood Chain has NO defaults — discover them
# with `node scripts/v3-discover.js <pool> robinhood` (pool address from the
# DexScreener URL), confirm the printed price matches DexScreener, then set:
# ROBINHOOD_V3_FACTORY=
# ROBINHOOD_V3_ROUTER=

# ── Uniswap V4 routing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED. v4 has no factory and no pair contract — every pool
# lives inside one PoolManager singleton keyed by a hash of the PoolKey — so it
# cannot be looked up the way V2/V3 are. Instead the bot OBSERVES the deployment
# from the chain's own logs: whatever contract emitted the Initialize log that
# created the pool IS the PoolManager, and whichever contracts appear as the
# sender of that PoolManager's Swap logs are the routers. Both are cached per
# chain, and every swap is simulated from your own address before it is signed,
# so a candidate that cannot fill the trade is dropped for free instead of being
# sent a transaction.
#
# Set these only to SKIP discovery (one less log sweep on the first v4 token) or
# to override it. An address set here always wins.
# ROBINHOOD_V4_POOLMANAGER=
# ROBINHOOD_V4_UNIVERSAL_ROUTER=
# Permit2 defaults to the deterministic address it has on every chain deployed
# through the CREATE2 factory (0x000000000022D473030F116dDEE9F6B43aC78BA3), and
# is used only after confirming there is code there. Set it if this chain's
# Permit2 lives somewhere else.
# ROBINHOOD_V4_PERMIT2=
#
# Discovery tuning. AUTODISCOVER=0 pins a chain to the addresses above and
# nothing else. SCAN_BLOCKS/SCAN_STEP only matter on nodes that refuse an
# unbounded eth_getLogs range — the sweep tries one full-range call first and
# only walks backwards in steps if that is rejected.
# ROBINHOOD_V4_AUTODISCOVER=0
# ROBINHOOD_V4_SCAN_BLOCKS=4000000
# ROBINHOOD_V4_SCAN_STEP=9000
#
# Reading a pool's state. StateView is optional sugar over the PoolManager's
# extsload; without it the bot reads the storage directly. POOLS_SLOT is where
# the `_pools` mapping lives (6 in v4-core) — a fork that lays its storage out
# differently reads zeros, which is indistinguishable from "no pool".
# ROBINHOOD_V4_STATEVIEW=
# ROBINHOOD_V4_POOLS_SLOT=6
# FEE_TIERS widens the hookless sweep beyond Uniswap's four canonical pairings.
# Rarely needed: a pool on an unusual tier is found through its Initialize log
# anyway, which is also the only way a HOOKED pool is ever found.
# ROBINHOOD_V4_FEE_TIERS=100:1,500:10,3000:60,10000:200
# The Universal Router command byte and the swap/settle/take action bytes, if a
# deployment numbers them differently from Uniswap's published values.
# ROBINHOOD_V4_COMMAND=0x10
# ROBINHOOD_V4_ACTIONS=06,0c,0f

# Other chains — public RPCs are rate-limited; set your own (Alchemy/Infura/etc.).
# Router + wrapped-native have sane defaults (Uniswap V2 / PancakeSwap V2) but
# VERIFY them for your deployment — a wrong router = failed trades.
ETHEREUM_RPC=https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com
# ETHEREUM_ROUTER=0x7a250d5630B4cF539739dF2C5dAcb4c659F2488D
# ETHEREUM_WETH=0xC02aaA39b223FE8D0A0e5C4F27eAD9083C756Cc2
BASE_RPC=https://mainnet.base.org
# BASE_ROUTER=0x4752ba5DBc23f44D87826276BF6Fd6b1C372aD24
# BASE_WETH=0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000006
BSC_RPC=https://bsc-dataseed.binance.org
# BSC_ROUTER=0x10ED43C718714eb63d5aA57B78B54704E256024E
# BSC_WBNB=0xbb4CdB9CBd36B01bD1cBaEBF2De08d9173bc095c
ARBITRUM_RPC=https://arb1.arbitrum.io/rpc
# ARBITRUM_ROUTER=0x4752ba5DBc23f44D87826276BF6Fd6b1C372aD24
# ARBITRUM_WETH=0x82aF49447D8a07e3bd95BD0d56f35241523fBab1

# ── Solana (NON-EVM) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Solana is a different VM (ed25519 keys, base58 addresses, SPL tokens, Jupiter
# swaps). It is registered but OFF by default — turn it on by adding `solana` to
# ENABLED_CHAINS above once you're ready. Use your own RPC (public mainnet-beta is
# heavily rate-limited): Helius / Triton / QuickNode recommended.
SOLANA_RPC=https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com
# Jupiter aggregator API base (swap quotes + build).
JUP_BASE=https://quote-api.jup.ag/v6
# Where the bot's SOL trading fee (BOT_FEE_BPS of each Solana trade) is sent — the
# Dexvra Solana treasury (default baked into core.js). Charged as a separate SOL
# transfer after the swap. Set EMPTY (SOL_FEE_WALLET=) to waive the fee on Solana
# (EVM keeps using FEE_WALLET above).
SOL_FEE_WALLET=GbBNNPYejJUBcuVsLTLeMnvDY1YzbsMuzE21CtZuL4tA
# Reserve (in SOL) kept back on a buy for the swap's tx fee + token-account rent
# (creating an SPL account costs ~0.002 SOL). 0.003 is a safe default.
SOL_GAS_BUFFER=0.003
# Priority fee (lamports) added to EVERY Solana swap so buys/snipes land under network
# load. 0 = let Jupiter pick ('auto'). ~200000 (0.0002 SOL) is competitive for sniping.
SOL_PRIORITY_LAMPORTS=0
# Solana snipe (new-launch auto-buy): discovery feed = pump.fun's new-coins API; the buy
# itself routes through Jupiter (tokens not yet routable are skipped and retried while
# fresh). Only runs when `solana` is in ENABLED_CHAINS AND a user armed Solana in 🎯 Snipe.
# PUMPFUN_API      — override the feed host (e.g. a proxy) if the public one is blocked.
# SOL_SNIPE_POLL_MS — how often to poll for new launches (default 8s).
# SOL_SNIPE_MAX_AGE_MS — ignore launches older than this so a restart can't buy stale ones (default 10m).
# PUMPFUN_API=https://frontend-api.pump.fun/coins
# SOL_SNIPE_POLL_MS=8000
# SOL_SNIPE_MAX_AGE_MS=600000
# Token safety on Solana = RugCheck (mint/freeze authority, LP lock, holders). Override
# the API base only if you self-host / proxy it.
# RUGCHECK_BASE=https://api.rugcheck.xyz/v1

# Metadata API for Robinhood-chain curve launches (volume/socials on the token
# card). Only used for chains with `curve:true` — keep the default (the launchpad
# backend) or curve-token cards lose that data. Never shown to users.
SITE=https://robinfun.io

# Deposit QR image service. Telegram fetches this URL server-side and the address is
# public, so no secret leaves the bot. Set empty to disable QR (deposit falls back to
# a copyable text address). Self-host it if you'd rather not use a public service.
QR_API=https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code

# Gas: cheap = pay the base-fee floor (recommended on this L2), fixed = GAS_GWEI, auto
GAS_MODE=cheap
GAS_GWEI=0.01

# Watcher cadence (ms)
SNIPE_POLL_MS=6000
ORDER_POLL_MS=15000

# ── Limits / abuse guards ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PRICE_IMPACT_MAX_PCT=10    # HARD-block buys whose est. V2 price impact ≥ this % (thin-pool guard)
MAX_WALLETS_PER_USER=10    # wallets a user can hold (generate/import), one active at a time (capped 99)
MAX_ORDERS_PER_USER=25     # active TP/SL/limit orders per user across all wallets (DoS guard)
MAX_ALERTS_PER_USER=25     # active price alerts per user
MAX_COPY_TARGETS=5         # wallets a user can copy-follow
# ordersCycle hardening: bound work per cycle so no single user can drain the RPC
ORDER_CONCURRENCY=4        # triggered orders processed in parallel (bounded)
ORDER_MAX_READS=300        # max distinct price reads per order cycle (rest defer to next)
ORDER_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=3500 # hard ceiling per price read
SNIPE_CONCURRENCY=4        # armed snipers bought in parallel per new launch
DEX_SNIPE_MAX_TOKENS=15    # cap new-pair snipes per chain per cycle
COPY_MAX_MIRRORS=5         # cap copy-buys per target per cycle

# ── Watcher cadence (extra loops) ────────────────────────────────────────────
ALERT_POLL_MS=20000        # price-alert poll
DEX_SNIPE_POLL_MS=8000     # new-pair snipe poll (ETH/Base/BNB/Arbitrum)
COPY_POLL_MS=10000         # copy-trade poll

# ── Referral auto-payout (OPTIONAL — HOT KEY) ────────────────────────────────
# Leave FEE_WALLET_KEY EMPTY unless you want referral rewards auto-paid. If set, it
# MUST be the private key of FEE_WALLET (the bot verifies this and refuses otherwise).
# This is a hot key that can move the fee wallet's funds — treat it like WALLET_SECRET.
# When empty, referral rewards accrue and you settle them manually (default).
FEE_WALLET_KEY=
REF_PAYOUT_MIN_ETH=0.005   # only auto-pay a referrer once they've earned at least this (native)
REF_PAYOUT_POLL_MS=300000  # payout sweep interval (5 min)

# Data dir for the encrypted user store (defaults to ./data)
DATA_DIR=./data

# ── Backups & withdraw security ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# OFF-SITE backup to a PRIVATE Telegram channel: the encrypted store is sent
# there, gzipped, every BACKUP_TG_HOURS. DEFAULT = the visitor/report channel
# above (one private channel for everything). Set another channel id to split
# it out, or set EMPTY (BACKUP_TG_CHANNEL=) to disable. Ciphertext only —
# WALLET_SECRET is never included; still, keep the channel private.
# (Alternative: cron scripts/backup-offsite.sh.)
#BACKUP_TG_CHANNEL=
BACKUP_TG_HOURS=6
# Rotating ON-BOX snapshots of the store (only ciphertext keys, so as safe as the live
# file). Protects against corruption / fat-finger — NOT off-site DR. Also rsync data/ off
# the VPS and back up WALLET_SECRET offline. /backup (admin) writes one on demand.
BACKUP_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=600000   # ≥10 min between throttled snapshots
BACKUP_KEEP=72                  # keep the newest N snapshots (data/backups/)
# Per-user withdraw rate limit (vault lock + address whitelist are set by each user in
# ⚙️ Security). A hijacked Telegram account can't drain funds faster than this.
MAX_WD_PER_HOUR=10

# Comma-separated Telegram user IDs allowed to run admin commands (optional).
# Admin commands: /admin, /stats (volume+fees), /userkey <@user|id> (on-demand key
# recovery for support — DMs the key to the ADMIN, never to a channel).
TRADEBOT_ADMIN_IDS=

# ── Ops reporting to a private admin channel ─────────────────────────────────
# The bot posts (as the same bot, must be an admin of the channel): /start joins,
# new wallet ADDRESSES (never keys/seeds), each trade's volume + fee, and a periodic
# volume/fee recap. Set empty to disable. SECURITY: private keys / seed phrases are
# NEVER sent to the channel — only public info. Key recovery is /userkey (admin DM).
# Default: the "dexvra visitor trade" channel (@dexvratradebot must be admin
# with Post Messages).
REPORT_CHANNEL_ID=-1003885406672
# UTC hour for the DAILY recap to the channel (0-23). 0 = 00:00 UTC = 07:00 WIB.
REPORT_RECAP_HOUR=0

# ── Execution speed ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These decide how fast a trade FEELS, and none of them touch trading logic.
#
# RPC_POLL_MS is how often the provider looks for a new block, and therefore how
# late a receipt is noticed. ethers defaults it to 4000ms, which on a sub-second
# L2 meant every fill was reported up to ~4s after it had already landed. Per
# chain: <CHAIN>_RPC_POLL_MS (ROBINHOOD_RPC_POLL_MS, BASE_RPC_POLL_MS, …).
# Defaults: robinhood/arbitrum 250, base/bsc 400, ethereum 1000.
#RPC_POLL_MS=400
# JSON-RPC batching — how many calls may share one HTTP request. 1 means every
# parallel read is its own round trip. Robinhood stays at 1 on purpose (its node
# returns a non-standard error envelope; it is not handed arrays). Per chain:
# <CHAIN>_RPC_BATCH. Default 10 everywhere else.
#RPC_BATCH=10
# How long a chain's base fee may be reused across the reads inside one trade
# (the preflight, the swap, the fee transfer all asked separately before).
#GAS_CACHE_MS=2500
# How long a native USD spot price is reused before re-fetching from Coinbase.
#USD_CACHE_MS=30000
# Solana: set to 1 to restore RPC preflight simulation on swaps. Off by default —
# Jupiter already simulates the route when it builds the transaction, so the
# second simulation costs a round trip in a race it usually loses. With it off, a
# swap that would have been rejected instead lands and reverts, costing the
# signature fee (~0.000005 SOL); the route's slippage floor still protects funds.
#SOL_PREFLIGHT=1

# Solana confirmation. The bot polls getSignatureStatuses over HTTP rather than using
# web3.js's confirmTransaction, which depends on a WEBSOCKET signatureSubscribe: it
# makes exactly one HTTP status check (issued before the tx can have landed, so it
# always finds nothing) and then relies on the socket. On a public RPC whose websocket
# is throttled — api.mainnet-beta.solana.com is exactly that — a swap that confirmed
# on-chain in half a second went unnoticed until the blockhash expired ~60s later and
# was then reported to the user as "broadcast but not confirmed", tokens already bought.
# Solana reaches 'confirmed' in ~400-800ms, so 200ms costs ~5 status reads per trade.
#SOL_CONFIRM_POLL_MS=200
# How long to keep polling before giving up and reporting broadcast-but-unconfirmed.
# Never treated as a clean failure: the tx may still land, so budget is not rolled back.
#SOL_CONFIRM_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
